{"parentUuid":"45d660f6-b807-4409-bea6-c9ae477a4568","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a57634746329618e2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019HuWAr8Ld9cuGxHFt2r5v1","type":"tool_result","content":"gameplay-architect ['C-ID', 'C-FRAME', 'C-TASK', 'C-ECS?', 'C-INPUT?', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-ANIM?', 'C-AUDIO?', 'C-NET?', 'C-REP?', 'C-WORLD?', 'C-SAVE?', 'C-UI?', 'C-VIEW?', 'C-A11Y', 'C-AIAGENT?'] [] ['C-GAME']\n    Gameplay framework: rules, players and possession, extension points and game-module structure, game flow and transitions, local players.\n   NR [['Abilities/tags/volumes toolkit', 'gameplay-systems-toolkit'], ['Scripting VM', 'scripting-runtime'], ['Game-specific code', 'external:game-team']]\ngameplay-systems-toolkit ['C-GAME', 'C-VIEW', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-ANIM?', 'C-AUDIO?', 'C-DEVICE?', 'C-PREDICT?', 'C-REP?', 'C-INPUT?', 'C-GAMEDATA', 'C-A11Y'] ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST'] []\n    Reusable gameplay systems: abilities, effects and attributes, gameplay tags, camera system, spawning and pooling, gameplay message routing, photo mode.\n   NR [['Generic events', 'entity-object-model'], ['Cinematic cameras', 'cinematics-sequencer']]\ncharacter-movement ['C-GAME', 'C-PHYS', 'C-INPUT', 'C-ANIM?', 'C-PREDICT?', 'C-DET'] [] ['C-MOVE']\n    Character movement as one system at the junction of input, physics, animation and netcode: movement modes, step/slope rules, root-motion consumption and authority, networked predicted/reconciled movement with a resimulatable move API, mount/vehicle transitions, 2D platformer movement.\n   NR [['Collide-and-slide controller primitive', 'character-physics'], ['Generic prediction machinery', 'prediction-rollback'], ['Animation selection', 'motion-synthesis']]\npersistence-save ['C-SER', 'C-ID', 'C-SVC?', 'C-WORLD?', 'C-CFG'] [] ['C-SAVE']\n    Save-game model and serialization, save versioning and migration, atomic writes, platform save APIs and quotas, cloud-save sync, persistent world-state deltas, checkpoints.\n   NR [['Schema evolution mechanism', 'serialization-schema'], ['Cloud service API', 'platform-services']]\ninput-system ['C-DEVICE?', 'C-FRAME', 'C-SER', 'C-A11Y'] [] ['C-INPUT']\n    Action-level input: mapping and context stacks, rebinding, buffering and latency accounting, local-multiplayer assignment, accessibility input options, UI navigation routing, per-device glyphs, recording and replay.\n   NR [['Device drivers and haptics', 'input-devices-haptics'], ['UI focus logic', 'ui-architect']]\neditor-architect ['C-REFL', 'C-SER', 'C-ASSET', 'C-WORLD', 'C-PLUGIN', 'C-UI?', 'C-IPC', 'C-NET?', 'C-REP?'] [] ['C-EDCMD']\n    Editor architecture: process model (in- vs out-of-process runtime), editor/runtime data separation, transactions and undo/redo, selection, extension API and tool scripting, play-in-editor isolation, remote live editing, headless editor, large-project performance.\n   NR [['Panels and inspectors', 'editor-ui-framework'], ['World viewport tools', 'world-editor-viewport'], ['Source control', 'collaboration-version-control']]\nfunctional-automation-soak ['C-GAME?', 'C-INPUT?', 'C-NET?'] [] []\n    Game-level automation: scripted and bot playthroughs, smoke/boot tests, soak and stability runs (memory growth, leaks), hardware/OS compatibility matrix, network harnesses and server load tests.\n   NR [['Unit test frameworks', 'test-architect'], ['Device-farm infrastructure', 'ci-cd-automation']]\nvisual-debugging-tools ['C-INSTR', 'C-ECS?', 'C-DRAW2D?', 'C-RSCENE?', 'C-REPLAY?', 'C-IPC'] [] ['C-DEVUI']\n    Debug draw API, in-game console and cheats, runtime entity inspector and gameplay debugger, visual logger and rewind, debug menus and overlays.\n   NR [['Logging and traces', 'observability-telemetry'], ['Render buffer visualization', 'render-architect']]\nplatform-web ['C-PAL'] [] []\n    Web target (WASM + WebGPU): threads and cross-origin isolation, memory limits, OPFS/IndexedDB storage, HTTP streaming delivery, user-gesture rules for audio/pointer/fullscreen, browser transport constraints.\n   NR [['WebGPU backend', 'rhi-webgpu'], ['Browser transports', 'network-transport']]\nobservability-telemetry ['C-PAL', 'C-BASE', 'C-SYNC'] [] ['C-INSTR']\n    Instrumentation substrate: structured logging, trace zones (CPU, GPU, IO, memory), counters and metrics, profiler integrations, in-game stats, development and live telemetry with privacy consent; zero cost when compiled out.\n   NR [['Crash capture', 'crash-diagnostics'], ['Debug drawing and consoles', 'visual-debugging-tools'], ['Perf budgets', 'performance-architect']]\nworld-architect ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-RES', 'C-ECS?', 'C-VIEW', 'C-FRAME'] [] ['C-WORLD', 'C-SIGNIF', 'C-ENV']\n    World representation strategy (data-oriented, no universal scene graph), partitioning and streaming cells, streaming sources, HLOD strategy, simulation LOD and significance, large-world coordinate policy, level transitions, server-side world streaming.\n   NR [['World document format', 'world-data-model'], ['Transform math', 'spatial-transforms'], ['HLOD mesh generation', 'virtualized-geometry-lod']]\ndata/capabilities.json:813:       \"Friends, parties, invites & join-in-progress\",\ndata/capabilities.json:1173:       \"Implementation language(s), standard baseline & compiler feature policy (incl. C++26 adoption plan, coding standard)\",\ndata/capabilities.json:2582:       \"WLD.MODEL.travel\",\ndata/capabilities.json:2583:       \"Level transitions & seamless travel\",\ndata/capabilities.json:3477:       \"Shading language & dialect policy (HLSL-class baseline)\",\ndata/capabilities.json:4537:       \"GPU feature-tier model & API baselines per hardware tier (C-GPUTIER)\",\ndata/capabilities.json:6179:       \"Seamless dynamic server meshing / cross-server entity authority\",\ndata/capabilities.json:8705:       \"QA.AGENT.baseline-governance\",\ndata/capabilities.json:9018:       \"PRF.GPU.baselines\",\ndata/capabilities.json:9019:       \"Automated GPU capture & per-pass cost baselines\",\ndata/capabilities.json:9116:       \"Transition peak analysis (travel, cutscene preload, cell churn)\",\ndata/contracts.json:833:   \"summary\": \"Named GPU feature tiers (binding model, pipeline-state model, queue topology, mesh/RT/tensor support, memory model) and the API baseline each tier maps to; render features declare the minimum tier they need.\",\ndata/milestones.json:111:   \"exit\": \"The indie-2d reference game is shippable on PC with editor, save, localization, accessibility baseline and hot reload; indie-2d-tools configuration builds.\",\ndata/radar.json:443:   \"tech\": \"Seamless server meshing\",\ndata/skills.json:5998:   \"purpose\": \"GPU platform architecture shared by every renderer tier: layering of RHI, GPU memory, render graph, shader system, ray-query and inference infrastructure; the GPU feature-tier model (binding, pipeline-state, queue\ndata/skills.json:6096:   \"purpose\": \"Implements C-RHI on Vulkan (profiles incl. Android Baseline, descriptor buffers/heaps, synchronization2, dynamic rendering); owns its validation-layer runs and vendor/driver quirks.\",","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9c7f0e92-156d-482c-80b4-a046508db928","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:20:17.717Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"45d660f6-b807-4409-bea6-c9ae477a4568","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
