{"parentUuid":"0a835c83-28d9-470b-9553-32518ded0fdb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a57634746329618e2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U6cy2Uwh6u3iQ7tgrQ73YA","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/00-design-principles.md:35:**Workstreams** (foundation, platform, content, world, rendering, simulation, audio, online, gameplay, UI, tools, release, quality, performance, governance) group skills for delegated arbitration and staffing. A dispute inside one lead's subtree is settled by that lead. Only cross-workstream disputes reach `engine-architect` (`ARCH.ORG.escalation`).\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:43:- **Tool code stays on the tool side.** Tool contracts (L5) may only be consumed from `tool_consumes`, so editor code can never enter a shipping or server build.\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:68:- **Scale/feature profiles.** A base profile (`minimal`, `min2d`, `lite3d`, `std3d`) plus add-ons (`openworld`, `online`, `aaa`, `xr`, `ugc`, `massim`, `sandbox`, `vehicles`, `team-large`).\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:69:- **A build target.** `client`, `headless-client`, `server` or `tools`.\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:70:- **Target platforms.** `pc`, `console`, `mobile`, `web`, `xr-standalone` or `server-host`.\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:72:Round 0 mixed these three axes. That made it impossible to express, for example, the server half of an open-world game or a 2D indie game shipping on console.\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:74:`check.py` proves all 22 named configurations are closed. These run from `minimal-client` (66 build skills) and `indie-2d-online-moddable-server` (53) up to `aaa-open-world-online-tools` (114). Capability-level profile tags provide finer gating inside a skill:\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:113:| `render-2d-vector` is the draw backend for 2D games, UI and developer overlays. `visual-debugging-tools` owns the in-game developer UI (`C-DEVUI`). | One batching, SDF and vector technique set. Developer UI must exist in development builds on every target, including servers. |\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:114:| Input is split into devices (`C-DEVICE`) and actions (`C-INPUT`). The action schema and tick-stamped command frames exist on every target. | Servers simulate from networked input commands; device binding exists only on clients. |\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:116:| First-party platform services (`platform-services`) are separate from third-party and live-ops backends (`online-services-liveops`). | The first is NDA SDKs plus certification. The second is web-service and live-operations engineering. |\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:117:| `ml-inference-runtime` owns standalone networks (`C-ML` for CPU/NPU, `C-MLGPU` for render-graph passes). `shader-system` owns in-shader neural evaluation. | One runtime keeps a single budget for standalone networks. Fused networks are shader code, and their cost belongs to the pass that hosts them. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:20:| A5 | Spatially sharded multi-server worlds (\"server meshing\") | Few shipped examples, sparse technical publication, and high vendor marketing content. | network-architect | Keep as `emerging`. The replication contract must not preclude authority transfer. Revisit when two or more shipped titles publish technical postmortems. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:29:| A15 | Dedicated-server world streaming and persistence boundary | Little published about server-side cell activation and write-behind persistence for open worlds. | world-architect, dedicated-server | Spike on the aaa-open-world-online-server configuration with bot clients (online-3d-bot-client). |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:45:| B8 | Scripting | Luau/Lua vs .NET (C#) vs Wasm vs visual-only vs none | scripting-runtime | Console AOT constraints, sandboxing (mods), iteration speed, GC pauses, team skills. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:47:| B10 | Netcode model | Server-authoritative + prediction vs rollback vs lockstep vs hybrid | network-architect | Genre, player count, determinism budget, bandwidth. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:57:| B20 | Transform/LWC representation | 64-bit world positions everywhere vs cell-relative 32-bit + origin rebasing | world-architect, spatial-transforms | World size, physics/GPU precision, network quantization. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:61:| B24 | Server scale-out | Single-server vs zoning/instancing vs seamless meshing | network-architect, dedicated-server | Player density, world size, authority-transfer cost; meshing stays experimental. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:62:| B25 | Gameplay control model | Possession-style controller/pawn vs data-oriented control binding vs genre-specific | gameplay-architect | Genre, multiplayer model, input-to-entity cardinality. |\ndocs/08-phase-2-plan.md:39:| Scalability validation | behavior per configuration (`indie-2d` … `aaa-open-world-online`, `dedicated-server`) |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6eac231f-9e08-4a7d-bfe6-8e7fdb1530bd","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:20:59.026Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0a835c83-28d9-470b-9553-32518ded0fdb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
